    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several favorable matchups today, with **Kyle Tucker** (77.49) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) leading the charge. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive 17% SP skill advantage against Lorenzen, while **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable 4.98 xERA matchup; the latter is particularly exciting as the 100% stolen base efficiency against a slow delivery from Gallen makes him a prime target for our scarcity-driven strategy. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) also cracks the elite tier, bolstered by a 14% platoon edge against Imai and a prime #2 spot in the order. Similarly, **Andy Pages** (70.21) thrives on the same SP skill boost as **Kyle Tucker**, positioning the outfield as the engine of our daily performance.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Jorge Polanco**, who provided a respectable 54.80 score but ultimately fell short against the high-floor production of **Coby Mayo** (55.38). While **Jorge Polanco** has a decent matchup, **Coby Mayo** benefits from a strong park factor and a solid platoon edge against Boyd, making him the preferred choice in the UTIL slot. We are monitoring the weather closely, as **Gunnar Henderson** (56.35) and **Coby Mayo** (55.38) face a 45% rain risk in their game against Boyd, and **Drake Baldwin** (43.12) carries a 33% risk against Skenes. Despite the talent of **Miguel Vargas** (53.67) and his elite xwOBA, his platoon disadvantage against Tolle kept him off the board in favor of our higher-efficiency starters. Expect an aggressive approach on the basepaths today, provided the skies hold.",
